                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ea76ec28-3a7f-39c4-bf3f-258234cb2a03",
                        "entry_id": "31c4ac8e-be57-389d-999e-ca001967aa74",
                        "glosses": [
                            "разг. делать небольшие углубления в чем-либо, ковырять что-либо"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "656e5401-0e45-458e-bdd5-a04f5f4eeca9",
                                "sense_id": "ea76ec28-3a7f-39c4-bf3f-258234cb2a03",
                                "text": "Погода супер, я очень надеюсь, что она продержится до вечера субботы, а потом хоть потоп, неохота в грязи колупаться."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "36d78fd8-dd3e-30de-ba82-c9fce5757d3c",
                        "entry_id": "31c4ac8e-be57-389d-999e-ca001967aa74",
                        "glosses": [
                            "разг. делать что-либо неторопливо, медленно; возиться, копаться"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7ad92cf3-e523-4518-a1a8-66081b4b1018",
                                "sense_id": "36d78fd8-dd3e-30de-ba82-c9fce5757d3c",
                                "text": "Нужна добротная машинка, чтоб особо не колупаться, небольшая, так как недавно начал ездить. Я сам люблю колупаться с гитарами, только приходится на мелочи очень много времени тратить (в основном на перепайку электроники, разные модернизации)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "91b8d789-3d6d-4c85-ab61-ed3814dec213",
                                "sense_id": "36d78fd8-dd3e-30de-ba82-c9fce5757d3c",
                                "text": "Теперь колупаемся, а потом спешку будем пороть."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4c37c139-703c-40cf-8a78-9de01082232b",
                        "source_entry_id": "31c4ac8e-be57-389d-999e-ca001967aa74",
                        "source_sense_description": "~ ковырять",
                        "target_lang_word": "delve",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "delve",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ce69399c-17b8-32c4-8180-e6a72deaa5b0",
                                        "entry_id": "bf249357-3735-3310-9db1-cf914c420d69",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To dig into the ground, especially with a shovel."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "45f967dc-58a4-43ae-9281-b67722ec0366",
                                                "sense_id": "ce69399c-17b8-32c4-8180-e6a72deaa5b0",
                                                "text": "Delve of convenient depth your thrashing floor."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1a570c4a-e0e8-45c6-a5d9-757d0eb4aa73",
                                                "sense_id": "ce69399c-17b8-32c4-8180-e6a72deaa5b0",
                                                "text": "I got a spade from the tool-house, and began to delve with all my might—it scraped the coffin; I fell to work with my hands; the wood commenced cracking about the screws; I was on the point of attaining my object, when it seemed that I heard a sigh from some one above, close at the edge of the grave, and bending down."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "118179d3-6fc1-4527-8590-de0bc0b13c21",
                                                "sense_id": "ce69399c-17b8-32c4-8180-e6a72deaa5b0",
                                                "text": "He finds out, soon enough for his weal and his bane, that he is stronger than Nature: and right tyrannously and irreverently he lords it over her, clearing, delving, dyking, building, without fear or shame."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1ceb6ff2-8bc3-48e7-9752-d03d56637e7b",
                                                "sense_id": "ce69399c-17b8-32c4-8180-e6a72deaa5b0",
                                                "text": "With a grunt that rejected a disgraceful admission of poverty, Bradly delved up a shilling and a sixpence and showed them to her. \"That's all I got left,\" he said, and tossed the coins dyspeptically away."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "039c49b1-1cee-382f-9159-e517ed44ae88",
                                        "entry_id": "bf249357-3735-3310-9db1-cf914c420d69",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To search thoroughly and carefully for information, research, dig into, penetrate, fathom, trace out"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "ambitransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "96678232-ebcc-4c8a-a135-a0fa63cd5e77",
                                                "sense_id": "039c49b1-1cee-382f-9159-e517ed44ae88",
                                                "text": "I cannot delve him to the root."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ab4af3ce-f6c7-435f-8ae9-7dd6e04831bd",
                                                "sense_id": "039c49b1-1cee-382f-9159-e517ed44ae88",
                                                "text": "She was intensely eager to delve into the mystery of Mr. Joplin and his brief case."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "940209e7-b284-4434-89cc-557932e3133e",
                                                "sense_id": "039c49b1-1cee-382f-9159-e517ed44ae88",
                                                "text": "Hampton delves into all sortsa cultural rootage — from country blues to smarmy Broadway show-tunage, combining them in a friendly, swinging way. This is the sorta record that should appeal to anybody who gave up on Zappa after Weasels Ripped My Flesh."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "03d07ee2-4c54-3793-ba0f-8d5982980c48",
                                        "entry_id": "bf249357-3735-3310-9db1-cf914c420d69",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To dig; to excavate."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "ambitransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b0ad9bdd-6e48-4402-985b-6370e1b9d17a",
                                                "sense_id": "03d07ee2-4c54-3793-ba0f-8d5982980c48",
                                                "text": "And then they made an oratory behind the altar, and would have dolven for to have laid the body in that oratory […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1f68f398-bae7-4903-ab1f-f85a62b50673",
                                                "sense_id": "03d07ee2-4c54-3793-ba0f-8d5982980c48",
                                                "text": "They dolve a grave beneath the arrow / And covered it with brere."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1bbaaad2-21b8-4367-8abc-27642d964110",
                                                "sense_id": "03d07ee2-4c54-3793-ba0f-8d5982980c48",
                                                "text": "Let him take off his plates and delve himself, if delving must be done."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "delve",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "917f2a69-2cdf-3d05-b81b-997798e902ad",
                                        "entry_id": "0139c8be-49f6-33cb-9ddb-7e60cd0c5c9d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A pit or den."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1504673a-e795-4b10-8dff-d0a191a45a4b",
                                                "sense_id": "917f2a69-2cdf-3d05-b81b-997798e902ad",
                                                "text": "the wise Merlin whylome wont (they say) / To make his wonne, low vnderneath the ground, / In a deepe delue, farre from the vew of day [...]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d1d2651e-6a42-4d3a-af08-1d15178454a5",
                                                "sense_id": "917f2a69-2cdf-3d05-b81b-997798e902ad",
                                                "text": "I put the clods on top the delve and gave it all a good thumping down with my feet."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
